Subject: [PATCH] fritchii-shadowmore: register shadow forms for IMAD cbuf/uniform, LOP3.LUT cbuf/uniform, ATOMG and

fritchii-shadowmore: register shadow forms for IMAD cbuf/uniform, LOP3.LUT cbuf/uniform, ATOMG and
TXD, and the bit-32 register check for ATOMG and TXD.
Switch EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_SHADOWMORE=1, off by default (Common::PeSwitch).

Upstream:
- zortos293/Lichii#279: IMAD 0xa24/0xc24 (constant buffer / uniform multiplier) shadow forms; two
  Kakariko graveyard pixel programs rejected, logged on an RX 9060 XT under RADV, a tombstone
  missing. Fritchii has 0xa24 only (register_pressure.h, with 0xa23/0x623/0x423).
- Frizti/Fritchii dd83423533 (#241, cherry-pick of f2960358b8): LOP3.LUT 0xa12/0xc12 (constant
  buffer / uniform B) shadow forms; in Ocarina both rejected pixel shaders of the Gerudo Valley rock
  draws, so the rocks were skipped and the sky showed through.
- Frizti/Fritchii 06bb2da979 (#588, imports #189 by vouion, cherry-pick of 33acb0e1a0): ATOMG
  0x9a8 and TXD 0xb6c/0xf6c shadow forms, and their bits 32-39 are checked against the mirrors.

What: the Ampere lowering shadows native registers that sit in its uniform mirrors and scratch
(R216-R246 and up). An instruction form missing from PrepareRegisterPressure gets the program
rejected ("native program uses lowering scratch registers") and its draws skipped ("Draw skipped
(no pipeline)"). For TXD and ATOMG the operand at bit 32 was never checked, so a gradient or data
register inside the mirrors silently read the mirror's value instead.

Operand sets (same as Fritchii v5 register_pressure.h): 0xa24/0xc24/0xa12/0xc12 Rd(16), A(24),
C(64); 0x9a8 Rd(16), data(32); 0xb6c/0xf6c Rd pair(16), coordinates (24, three registers for
ARRAY_2D: Bits(61,3) == 5), four gradients (32), second destination pair (64).

Unset: the new cases return valid = false exactly like the default case, and the bit-32 test is
unchanged, so lowering is byte-identical.

Not needed here: #241's retry with a realigned high uniform base (our shadow_boundary is already
aligned down to four, lower_to_maxwell.h:280). SHF 0x219 (#241's other form) is already in as 0346
behind EDEN_UP_SHADOW_REGISTERS (Gerudo Valley needs both switches). The lowering of these opcodes
already exists (0xc24 at :732, 0xa24 :887, 0xb6c :1182, 0x9a8 :1400, 0xa12/0xc12 :3030); 0xf6c
has no lowering here, so its shadow form is inert until one is added (kept to match upstream).

With the switch on, a TXD/ATOMG whose register is in the mirrors and cannot be shadowed now gets
the program rejected (draw skipped) instead of reading a wrong value. Catch2 tests not ported.

PS5: low value now (513 logs from 6-9 Nov, Kokiri/pond/walks, show no rejection of these opcodes),
real from Kakariko (graveyard tombstone) and Gerudo Valley (rocks, with EDEN_UP_SHADOW_REGISTERS=1).

diff --git a/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h b/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h
index f13f8c6..57951d0 100644
--- a/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h
+++ b/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h
@@ -108,6 +108,28 @@ inline RegisterPressure PrepareRegisterPressure(const Instruction& input, u32 re
     case 0xa20: case 0x621: case 0x808: case 0x923: operand(16); operand(24); break;
     case 0x209: operand(16); operand(24); operand(32); break;
     case 0xa23: case 0x623: case 0x423: operand(16); operand(24); operand(64); break;
+    // EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_SHADOWMORE=1: shadow forms Fritchii/Lichii have and this table lacked.
+    // Unset: no shadow form, as before (the program is rejected and its draws skipped).
+    // IMAD with a constant buffer or uniform multiplier (zortos293/Lichii#279: two Kakariko
+    // graveyard pixel programs, logged on RADV) and LOP3.LUT with a constant buffer or uniform B
+    // (#241, Fritchii dd83423533: Gerudo Valley rocks): Rd, A and C, no register at bit 32.
+    case 0xa24: case 0xc24: case 0xa12: case 0xc12: {
+        static const bool enabled = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_SHADOWMORE");
+        if (!enabled) { result.valid = false; return result; }
+        operand(16); operand(24); operand(64); break;
+    }
+    case 0x9a8: { // ATOMG (#588, Fritchii 06bb2da979): result in Rd, data operand at bit 32.
+        static const bool enabled = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_SHADOWMORE");
+        if (!enabled) { result.valid = false; return result; }
+        operand(16); operand(32); break;
+    }
+    case 0xb6c: case 0xf6c: { // TXD (#588): Rd pair, coordinates (+ layer for ARRAY_2D),
+        // four gradients at bit 32, second destination pair.
+        static const bool enabled = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_SHADOWMORE");
+        if (!enabled) { result.valid = false; return result; }
+        operand(16, 2); operand(24, input.Bits(61, 3) == 5 ? 3 : 2); operand(32, 4); operand(64, 2);
+        break;
+    }
     case 0x321: operand(16, input.Bits(74, 2) + 1); operand(24); operand(32); break;
     case 0x322: operand(24); operand(32, input.Bits(74, 2) + 1); break;
     case 0x927: operand(24); operand(32); break;
@@ -306,10 +328,16 @@ inline LoweredProgram LowerToMaxwellWith(std::span<const Instruction> code, u32
         // that could alias that state go through shadow copies, or are rejected.
         RegisterPressure pressure{insn};
         bool requires_shadow = false;
+        // EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_SHADOWMORE=1 (#588, Fritchii 06bb2da979): TXD's gradients and ATOMG's
+        // data word sit at bits 32-39 too; unchecked, a register in the uniform mirrors read the
+        // mirror instead of its own value. Unset: not checked, as before.
+        static const bool shadow_more = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_SHADOWMORE");
+        const bool bit32_register =
+            shadow_more && (opcode == 0xb6c || opcode == 0xf6c || opcode == 0x9a8);
         for (u32 bit : {16U, 24U, 32U, 64U}) {
             if (bit == 32 && insn.Bits(9, 3) != 1 && opcode != 0xb60 && opcode != 0xb66 && opcode != 0xf66 &&
                 opcode != 0x988 && opcode != 0x986 && opcode != 0x927 && opcode != 0x98e &&
-                opcode != 0x59f) continue;
+                opcode != 0x59f && !bit32_register) continue;
             const u32 reg = insn.Bits(bit, 8);
             if (reg >= shadow_boundary && reg < 255) requires_shadow = true;
         }
